    "knowledge_point": "Finding Solutions to Exponential Equations when Rearrangement is Required",
    "problem": "Given that ${e}^{-5z}-6=-2,$ find the value of $z$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.",
    "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5z}-6 & =-2 \\\\ {e}^{-5z} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5z} & =4 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{-5z}) & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ -5z & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z=-\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(4)$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nz≈-0.277\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
